lemma":"רְחוֹב","tr":"re·chov","gloss":"street","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":43},{"base":"H5975","lemma":"עָמַד","tr":"a·mad","gloss":"to stand: stand","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":521},{"base":"H6605","lemma":"פָּתַח","tr":"pa·tach","gloss":"to open","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":144},{"base":"H5608","lemma":"סָפַר","tr":"sa·phar","gloss":"to recount","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":159}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1TI","chapter":2,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Therefore I want the men everywhere to pray, lifting up holy hands, without anger or dissension.","from":6},{"book":"LEV","chapter":23,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"“Speak to the Israelites and say, ‘On the first day of the seventh month you are to have a day of rest, a sacred assembly announced by trumpet blasts.","from":2},{"book":"EXO","chapter":4,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"and they believed. And when they heard that the LORD had attended to the Israelites and had seen their affliction, they bowed down and worshiped.","from":6},{"book":"EZR","chapter":7,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"this Ezra came up from Babylon. He was a scribe skilled in the Law of Moses, which the LORD, the God of Israel, had given. The king had granted Ezra all his requests, for the hand of the LORD his God was upon him.","from":1},{"book":"NEH","chapter":9,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"And the Levites—Jeshua, Bani, Kadmiel, Shebaniah, Bunni, Sherebiah, Bani, and Chenani—stood on the raised platform and cried out in a loud voice to the LORD their God.","from":7},{"book":"LAM","chapter":3,"verse":41,"verseEnd":41,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Let us lift up our hearts and hands to God in heaven:","from":6},{"book":"LUK","chapter":24,"verse":45,"verseEnd":45,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Then He opened their minds to understand the Scriptures.","from":8},{"book":"ACT","chapter":28,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"So they set a day to meet with Paul, and many people came to the place he was staying. He expounded to them from morning to evening, testifying about the kingdom of God and persuading them about Jesus from the Law of Moses and the Prophets.","from":8}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"9-12":{"people":[{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"ezra-h5830g","name":"Ezra","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"nehemiah-h5166h","name":"Nehemiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":9}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H6918","lemma":"קָדוֹשׁ","tr":"qa·dosh","gloss":"holy","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":116},{"base":"H0408","lemma":"אַל","tr":"al","gloss":"not","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":724},{"base":"H4490","lemma":"מָנָה","tr":"ma·nah","gloss":"portion","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":13},{"base":"H6087","lemma":"עָצַב","tr":"a·tsav","gloss":"to hurt","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":17},{"base":"H1058","lemma":"בָּכָה","tr":"ba·khah","gloss":"to weep","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":114},{"base":"H0995","lemma":"בִּין","tr":"bin","gloss":"to understand","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":170},{"base":"H8354","lemma":"שָׁתָה","tr":"sha·tah","gloss":"to drink","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":217},{"base":"H3881","lemma":"לֵוִי","tr":"le·viy·yi","gloss":"Levi","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":291},{"base":"H2304","lemma":"חֶדְוָה","tr":"ched·vah","gloss":"joy","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H4477","lemma":"מַמְתַֿקִּים","tr":"mam·taq","gloss":"sweetness","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":28,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":61,"source":"openbible","text":"The LORD is my strength and my shield; my heart trusts in Him, and I am helped. Therefore my heart rejoices, and I give thanks to Him with my song.","from":10},{"book":"PSA","chapter":28,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":61,"source":"openbible","text":"The LORD is the strength of His people, a stronghold of salvation for His anointed.","from":10},{"book":"PRO","chapter":17,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":41,"source":"both","text":"A joyful heart is good medicine, but a broken spirit dries up the bones.","from":10},{"book":"2CO","chapter":12,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":28,"source":"openbible","text":"Three times I pleaded with the Lord to take it away from me.","from":10},{"book":"2CO","chapter":12,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":28,"source":"openbible","text":"But He said to me, “My grace is sufficient for you, for My power is perfected in weakness.” Therefore I will boast all the more gladly in my weaknesses, so that the power of Christ may rest on me.","from":10},{"book":"ECC","chapter":9,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":24,"source":"both","text":"Go, eat your bread with joy, and drink your wine with a cheerful heart, for God has already approved your works:","from":10},{"book":"ISA","chapter":12,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":20,"source":"openbible","text":"In that day you will say: “O LORD, I will praise You. Although You were angry with me, Your anger has turned away, and You have comforted me.","from":10},{"book":"ISA","chapter":12,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":20,"source":"openbible","text":"With joy you will draw water from the springs of salvation,","from":10}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"persian-era","title":"Persian era: Esther and the return","people":2}]},"13-18":{"people":[{"id":"ezra-h5830g","name":"Ezra","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":1,"